     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, December 19, 2014 11:40:55 PM UTC+2, Winston Chang wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Chris - I just noticed this bug in the dev version and pushed a fix.</div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Dec 19, 2014 at 7:56 AM, Chris B. <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">christo...@googlemail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">A minimalistic example to illustrate the behaviour:<div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Server.R</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  output$val</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderPrint</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">null</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$rb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      updateRadioButtons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;rb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Radiobuttons&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> selected </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#if(input$rb == &quot;1&quot;) # This returns an error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#print(&quot;error&quot;)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    input$rb<br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># UI.R</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fluidPage</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  radioButtons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;rb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;RadioButtons&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> choices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> selected </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  textOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;val&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><br>Am Freitag, 19. Dezember 2014 14:43:25 UTC+1 schrieb Chris B.:<div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Please excuse if I missed some obvious changes to the functionality of radioButtons() or the shiny package in general.<div><br></div><div>After updating to the latest dev build of shiny I encounter the following problem:</div><div><br></div><div>The radioButtons() returns NULL when a shiny app is started, instead of the value determined by the &quot;selected&quot; parameter. </div><div>Even updateRadioButtons(session, ...) does not work and NULL is returned. Only manually clicking the radioButtons once does the trick.</div><div><br></div><div>This bevahiour breaks all logical statements as the length of input$radiobuttons is of length zero initially.</div><div><br></div><div>All packages are up-to-date. Session Info below.</div><div><br></div><div>Best</div><div><br></div><div>Christoph</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">R version </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2014</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31</s